  "raw_text": "{\n  \"options\": [\n    \"My first job at a pizza shop near home was tough. It was very hard work. On busy nights, we made dozens of pizzas in a few hours, and customers got mad if food was late. My boss, Tony, taught me to stay calm and focus on one thing. I also learned to talk to angry people without losing my temper. The job was tiring, but it taught me to handle stress better. These skills will help me in college and any job I have in the future.\",\n    \"When I started my first job at a pizza place near my house, I thought it would be easy. Instead, I quickly learned it was very hard work. On busy nights, we made dozens of pizzas in just a few hours, and customers got upset if their food was late. My manager, Tony, taught me how to stay calm and do one thing at a time. I also learned how to talk to people who were angry without getting angry myself. The job was tiring, but it showed me that I can handle stress better than I thought. These skills will help me in college and in any job I have in the future.\",\n    \"Last summer, I got my first job working at a small pizza restaurant near my house. At first I thought it would be easy, but I quickly found out that it was a lot of work. On busy nights we had to make dozens of pizzas in just a few hours, and customers got upset if their food was late. My manager, Tony, taught me how to stay calm and do one thing at a time. I also learned how to talk to people who were angry without getting angry myself. The job was tiring, but it showed me that I can handle stress better than I thought. These skills will help me in college and in any job I have in the future.\",\n    \"Last summer I got my first job working at a small pizza restaurant near my house. At first I thought it would be easy, but I quickly found out that it was a lot of work. On busy nights we had to make dozens of pizzas in just a few hours, and customers got upset if their food was late. My manager, Tony, taught me how to stay calm and do one thing at a time. I also learned how to talk to people who were angry without getting angry myself. The job was tiring, but it showed me that I can handle stress better than I thought. These skills will help me in college and in any job I have in the future.\",\n    \"Last summer I got my first job working at a small pizza restaurant near my house. At first I thought it would be easy, but I quickly found out that it was a lot of work. On busy nights we had to make dozens of pizzas in just a few hours, and customers got upset if their food was late. My manager, Tony, taught me how to stay calm and do one thing at a time. I also learned how to talk to people who were angry without getting angry myself. The job was tiring, but it showed me that I can handle stress better than I thought. These skills will help me in college and in any job I have in the future.\"\n  ]\n}\n",
